{"schema": 1, "kind": "resolution", "id": "rev-20261110T161036Z-785c5f8d:rev-20261110T160341Z-a0590c18:R-2", "ts": "2026-11-10T16:13:09Z", "actor": {"worktree": "prawduct", "plugin": "3.8.2-dev", "branch": "feature/audit-guidance", "build": "df208065877d+dirty"}, "body": {"finding": {"review_id": "rev-20261110T160341Z-a0590c18", "fid": "R-2"}, "disposition": "fixed", "verified_by": "rev-20261110T161036Z-785c5f8d", "at_tree": "539c89e997d1d503bbaa1e54d1ddb639d04a8a3c", "rationale": "Read plugin/methodology/delegation.md whole. 'Who does what' now says the integrator is the one delegate that leaves its scratch branch (git switch onto the integration branch, coordinator's checkout off it), and 'Dispatch and reaping' scopes the no-switch sentence to build delegates. Mechanism checked against code, not the prose: gitstate.ephemeral_kind_of returns None for an agent- directory on a non-scratch branch, so test-evidence record takes the full path (bin/prawduct-hook, scratch_kind is None) and appends a non-narrowed test-run fact that gates._store_run_vouching reads by tree, head and branch. building.md 'Who integrates', the project-preferences Delegation row and the digest line name the integrator without contradicting this."}}

